#=GF RT   HIV-1 TAR miRNA protects against apoptosis by altering cellular gene
#=GF RT   expression.
#=GF RA   Klase Z, Winograd R, Davis J, Carpio L, Hildreth R, Heydarian M, Fu S,
#=GF RA   McCaffrey T, Meiri E, Ayash-Rashkovsky M, Gilad S, Bentwich Z, Kashanchi F
#=GF RL   Retrovirology. 2009;6:18.
#=GF CC   This family represents the HIV trans-activation response (TAR) element
#=GF CC   which is known to be required for the trans-activation of the viral
#=GF CC   promoter and for virus replication. The TAR hairpin acts as a binding site
#=GF CC   for the Tat protein and this interaction stimulates the activity of the
#=GF CC   long terminal repeat promoter [1]. Further experiments have shown that TAR
#=GF CC   acts as a miRNA that protects against apoptosis [2,3].
#=GF WK   Trans-activation_response_element_(TAR)
